WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:04.112
The question comes first: product retention.

2
00:00:04.112 --> 00:00:09.966
Check the grain of the data and its definitions before you draw a chart or build a model.

3
00:00:10.366 --> 00:00:14.716
Use SQL to define the first active period for each customer.

4
00:00:14.716 --> 00:00:23.925
In Jupyter, build a retention matrix and check that each row uses the same cohort definition before comparing the percentages.

5
00:00:24.325 --> 00:00:28.814
Compare the cohort heatmap in Tableau with a Power BI summary.

6
00:00:28.814 --> 00:00:35.332
Inspect the operational signal in Grafana, then reconcile the underlying totals in Excel.

7
00:00:35.332 --> 00:00:39.677
The cohort definition must remain consistent in every view.

8
00:00:40.077 --> 00:00:42.491
Publish the story as cohort explorer.

9
00:00:42.491 --> 00:00:47.841
Let people filter the view, inspect the evidence, and understand the next action.

10
00:00:47.841 --> 00:00:52.473
The presentation should remain clear when the underlying data changes.
